# Premium visual quality

1B Run targets **professionally polished mobile sports-game UI**, not generic AI website design.

When the task involves UI, UX, layout, typography, color, splash, menus, motion, animation, or visual polish:

1. Read and follow project skills as needed:
   - `oneb-brand-visual` — brand lock (wins over generic design advice)
   - `premium-mobile-gaming-ui` — hierarchy, touch, spacing, depth
   - `cinematic-motion-graphics` — intentional motion; no dependency installs unless asked
   - `ios-visual-qa` — physical iPhone / Xcode as acceptance
2. Also use `frontend-design` for craft — but **never** override 1B Run tokens, Avenir stack, or arena identity.
3. GSAP + `@gsap/react` are installed — follow the `gsap-*` skills (useGSAP, scoped, contextSafe). Do not mix GSAP and Motion on one element.
4. Preserve established brand and existing functionality. Do not redesign unrelated screens.
5. Classify website / iOS / shared per `PLATFORM.md` before editing.
6. Final visual acceptance is the **physical iPhone build**, not localhost alone.
